\begin{abstract}
The Scientific Compressed Cosmos Vortex (SCCV-1) Engine is a sovereign
astrophysical computation platform integrating Einstein--Cartan torsion
gravity, Kerr--Cartan geodesic integration, post-quantum cryptography,
and hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) ingestion from LIGO and EHT-class
instrumentation. SCCV-1 performs encrypted tensor arithmetic using
CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024 and CKKS homomorphic evaluation while maintaining
real-time throughput on GPU clusters. This paper presents the unified
mathematical foundations, cryptographic architecture, hardware
integration pipeline, CUDA kernel suite, laboratory verification,
stress testing, and deployment strategy for SCCV-1.
\end{abstract}

